satoru gojo without any doubt  is one of the coolest anime characters  ever created  and yet what makes his character so  intriguing is not his unimaginable power  or his fantastic sense of humor  but the tragic irony that lies beneath  them  who then is satoru gojo what does it  mean to be  the strongest what is actually going on  behind those cold and clear eyes  and why does he have to cover them it's  time to find out  [Music]  rojo is the strongest curse user in  jiu-jitsu kaisen  akutami in taking inspiration from other  shonen stories  combines and expands upon them and  ultimately makes his characters  even more intriguing and fascinating  satoru gojo  is no exception here many traits of his  can  quite easily be traced back to other  popular shonen characters  but in the end he emerges as one of the  most  unique and complex personalities out  there  [Music]  if i had to pick one word to describe  satoru gojo  no doubt it would be strength gojo  is the pinnacle sorcerer of the ju-2  world he is to curses  what sukuna is to sorceress an  unbeatable force of nature that can at  best be hoped to be sealed away  but not actually killed beneath that  cool exterior  and immense power gojo's tragedy of a  character lies in his immeasurable  strength and how it determines  every aspect of his life as well as his  role in the story  being the strongest character he serves  as a signpost to both the audience  and the protagonists what is actually  possible in this world  and how far behind the other characters  actually still  are gojo's fighting style and the  respect and fear that he enjoys from  both friends and foes alike  is something we know from many other  anime netero  in hunter hunter shanks in one piece  shanks in fairy tale  or almighty and boku no hero like all of  them  goku has a very easy going boyish sort  of personality  that is immediately replaced by pure  strength and authority whenever his  patience is tested  he's the sort of character that almost  single-handedly holds the balance in the  worlds  without them chaos would erupt while  personality and look-wise goku could be  considered a cooler and more  entertaining version of kakashi  as a teacher he comes closer to all  might in that he's  not exactly the best at teaching but  still  good and thoughtful enough to grow the  next generation of  the quote-unquote good guys in fact gojo  has  quite a bunch of wonderful if admittedly  unconventional teaching moments  and while these mentor type of  characters usually feel like their best  days are already  over gojo very much seems to be in his  absolute prime when we first meet him in  the story  akutami makes it very clear very early  on  what gojo is actually capable of  building on sharp reflexes and a bright  tactical intellect  his ridiculous amount of cursed energy  and physical strength as well as his  capability to perform a complete domain  expansion  are only the tip of the iceberg gojo has  been blessed not only with  one but two inherited abilities that in  combination  make him more gods than men  the first of these is limitless an  ability that allows gojo to freely  manipulate  space and matter down to an atomic level  this allows him to slow down movement  and decide what can or cannot actually  touch him we can see this explained in  his fight with jogo in the most  hilarious way  [Music]  this ability makes it possible for gojo  to attract  and repulse matter giving him gravity  and anti-gravity attributes  the red and the blue his most  destructive skill however is combining  both of these attributes into hollow  purple which results in the complete  annihilation of any matter caught within  the attack  as if this wasn't scary enough though  gojo  also inherited the six ice an ability  that we honestly still know  very little about we do know however  that it allows him to perceive the world  around him in terms of mass  cursed energy and so on and so forth  making it the  perfect fit for limitless we can see  this ability in action for example  during the kyoto sister school exchange  event during the attack of hanami's  group on the school  not only was he immediately able to  pinpoint everyone's  exact location but he was also able to  easily assess the increase in ug's  cursed energy outputs  the in detail workings of these  abilities are actually incredibly  cleverly crafted  but not related to the main point of  this video so let me know in the  comments if you'd like to learn more  about gojo's limitless and the six eyes  the main takeaway point here is that  gojo has the one thing valued most in  the world of jujutsu  raw unmatched power this allows him to  shape the world around him in whatever  way he pleases  and this is what brings us into the  deeply nested  and layered realm of gojo satoru's  personality  due to his innate strength and claim to  authority gojo understandably is  extremely confident in his abilities to  the point where he believes himself to  be  invincible in relation to the central  moral argument of jujutsu kaisen  what constitutes a good life his view is  quite different from itadores  while itadore thinks that a good life  means enabling others to have  a good death for gojo the answer is  strength in essence when you have  strength you have  agency over the world your own life and  that of  others thus while yuji expresses his  belief in his hero complex  trying to save anyone weaker than him  and caring way too much about others  gojo is very self-centered and as we  will see  has difficulties understanding and  caring for people weaker than him for  instance he motivates megumi by telling  him to become stronger himself and less  reliant on  others  [Music]  and yet despite their polar views on  life surprisingly  in the end gojo and itadori have one of  the best relationships in the show  on the surface this seems to be due to  their similarly extroverted and  genuinely funny personalities  however both their god and hero complex  keep them from truly creating meaningful  relationships with others  as they can let themselves be vulnerable  by letting anyone come close enough to  help them in return or as gojo  formulates it  yuji and him always go for the home run  in that  sense while expressed in very different  ways both yuji  and gojo share the same fundamental  weakness  loneliness to fully understand gojo's  sense of loneliness we first have to  understand that despite his sense of  superiority  luckily for everyone around him he  actually has also a very strong sense of  morality  gojo cares about the well-being of  humanity and even more so for the people  close to him  however the society of jiu-jitsu  sorcerers in their commitment to  fighting the curses that threaten  humanity and human life  have ironically enough morphed into an  environment that is  incredibly dehumanizing in and of itself  all that matters are bloodlines  influence and  yes strength but despite being blessed  with the most desired trait amongst the  sorcerers  or maybe exactly because of it gojo  knows very well just  how corrupted the society has become his  big desire  and drive therefore is not to eradicate  all curses or something similar  but is pointed inward and aims at  revolutionizing the system of the juju  two world itself  and that's actually a very intriguing  desire for him to have  because it can't be solved by strength  alone  but requires the one thing that gojo  isn't great at  human relationships and comrades with a  common ideology  gojo knows this he doesn't want to be  the strongest forever  in fact he wants to be surpassed however  the main flaw in gojo's thinking is that  he can't help  but resemble the system that he was born  and raised in no matter how hard he  tries to struggle  he's still a part of the system he's  desperately trying to reform and so the  real problem that gojo faces  is that despite his self-centeredness  and his god complex  deep down this man has quite a big heart  and sense of morality that in the end  make him vulnerable hanami and jogo got  away because he prioritized yuji safety  over catching them mahito was able to  steal the cursed objects from the school  because gojo prioritized the lives of  his students  and determined that the true loss would  be their death  and so based on his emotional and  compassionate side  the region gojo feels so incredibly  lonely and isolated is  ironically enough his own strength and  power and i think nothing represents  this better than the key symbolism  of gojo's character his eyes  the reason he wears sunglasses like a  blind man and then  a literal blindfold later on is due to  the fact that he's always staring  into the infinity he always sees  everything this ability is of course  very tiring and the tragedy of it is  that gojo is literally  so good at seeing through people that  they  don't look like individuals to him  anymore every single person on earth is  filled with their own thoughts emotions  and biases  but gojo despite his six eyes doesn't  perceive that he only sees matter cursed  energy  speed and strength gojo has always  distant himself from both his own  feelings and the feelings of others  which then creates a divide between him  and the world around him  thus it's really hard for him to see  other people as  real people this distance to others  shines through in various ways  it's always gojo making the pop cultural  references for instance  [Music]  he was the one who taught ichidori to  literally handle his cursed energy  through his emotions by  literally forcing him to watch movies  and while i strongly believe that  stories are one of the most powerful  tools that we as human beings possess  having feelings due to perceived  strength and usefulness  is not quite the same thing as having  feelings and understanding a person  for who they really are gojole has thus  become a mere observer on the sideline  granted the ability to see everything  life became more of a movie than reality  with gojo being the only one in the  theater or as the master himself would  phrase it  thus gojo literally has to blind himself  and his powers in order to perceive  others as  actual people and i think it's fair to  call that  quite tragic however it also shows us  once again that gojo  really cares he cares that he can't see  people for who they are he cares that he  feels alone  and he cares that people suffer under  the current system  thus gojo willingly dampens his own  powers by blinding himself in order to  see others

